  },
  {
   "text": "On the same day Trump announces that top tech firms have signed an accord to \"self-police\" their own AI development, we learned that OpenAI employees and security researchers were reportedly ignored when they brought safety concerns to the company's top executives. \n\nSee the problem here?",
   "handle": "rbreich.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Robert Reich",
   "likes": 1080,
   "reposts": 489,
   "replies": 62,
   "created_at": "2026-09-30T15:31:03.082Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/rbreich.bsky.social/post/3mwqnyemj2k2o",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/29/technology/openai-warnings-security.html",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "A thing I learned not too long ago is that when an LLM selects a token that leads it down an incorrect path (factually), it has no way to back up, or even know that it should back up, it's just on to the next likely bit. Literally every LLM is just posting their way through it. What an image.",
   "handle": "scalzi.com",
   "display_name": "John Scalzi",
   "likes": 1233,
   "reposts": 182,
